data: {"type":"response.function_call_arguments.done","sequence_number":404,"item_id":"fc_08250c39c7e1fa30016ae21b12d3888191a1740ef08b49d2af","output_index":1,"arguments":"{\"pointer\":\"/nodes/P\",\"coverage\":\"assessed\",\"judgment\":{\"verdict\":\"PASS\",\"notes\":\"Independently compared the complete source with the inspected AuditBExport.P and Proof.lean:4–22,582–610. Positive natural dimensions represent exactly the positive integer dimensions. WSpace is the coordinate product (sup norm); its norm is equivalent to the Euclidean norm, preserving smoothness, compactness and coordinate derivatives. WTarget is EuclideanSpace, so its norms are the required Euclidean norms. Source-context D001–D004 specify exactly product Lebesgue volume, coordinate second derivatives, Frobenius density and the ordinary local time derivative. wDx evaluates fderiv on the coordinate unit vector, wT is the time derivative, wLap sums the repeated spatial derivatives, and wEnergy integrates wDensity without a half factor. H001–H006 retain all source assumptions: smoothness only on t>0, both unit conditions, pointwise existential normal scalar with no regularity, and one compact set per closed positive slab. Extending u arbitrarily to nonpositive times adds no restriction: positive points have neighborhoods inside wDomain, and restriction/extension preserves all these derivatives, density sections and integrals. The conclusion includes integrability, differentiability (not merely a totalized deriv equality), zero derivative for every t>0, and equality for all positive a,b, including a=b; no zero-time assertion. wGeometry/wLocal contain stronger derived facts, but are proved internally, not endpoint assumptions. Checked joint/slice derivative identifications in T003 and the coordinate splitting/insertion and measure-preserving conversions in T010–T011; there is no unproved representation bridge.\",\"locations\":[\"/endpoints/P/source\",\"/endpoints/P/actual\",\"/endpoints/P/correspondence\",\"/scope/full_target\",\"/scope/parameters\",\"/scope/hypotheses\",\"/documents/0\",\"/documents/2\"]}}"}

